{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.spectral_sequence_h3_explicit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.spectral_sequence_h3_explicit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.spectral_sequence_h3_explicit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.spectral_sequence_h3_explicit","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/spectral_sequence_h3_explicit.lean#L69-L88","doc":"**Content statement** (from manuscript):\n\nThis proposition computes the differentials $d_1, d_2$ of the\nGB-filtered Hochschild spectral sequence\n([GB spectral sequence](#prop:gb-spectral-sequence)) **explicitly**\non $H_3(R, q)$ over the paper's ground ring $R$ (paper's categorical base ring),\nmaking the page identifications\n([$E_\\infty$ page identifications](#prop:e-infinity-page-identifications))\nconcrete for the single-nucleon case.\n\n    The Lean encoding below states the manuscript claim over a context class and discharges it from the class's fields (§3b-conditional). The declaration type-checks as a complete term; the substantive mathematical content is carried by the context-class axioms, and a full derivation from substrate primitives remains pending. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:spectral-sequence-h3-explicit","label":"prop:spectral-sequence-h3-explicit","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-h3-explicit.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.claim_iii_page_identifications_concretised_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.claim_iii_page_identifications_concretised_holds","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/spectral_sequence_h3_explicit.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Witness for manuscript sub-claim (iii) — the `E_∞` page identifications\nare *concretised* on `H_3(R, q)` for the single-nucleon case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.claim_ii_d2_differential_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.claim_ii_d2_differential_holds","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/spectral_sequence_h3_explicit.lean#L64-L64","doc":"Witness for manuscript sub-claim (ii) — the explicit `d_2`-differential. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.claim_i_d1_differential_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.claim_i_d1_differential_holds","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/spectral_sequence_h3_explicit.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Witness for manuscript sub-claim (i) — the explicit `d_1`-differential\nof the GB-filtered Hochschild spectral sequence on `H_3(R, q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.HeckeH3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.HeckeH3","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/spectral_sequence_h3_explicit.lean#L59-L59","doc":"The Hecke algebra `H_3(R, q)` — abstract carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.claim_strand_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.claim_strand_count","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/spectral_sequence_h3_explicit.lean#L57-L57","doc":"Manuscript fact (encoded in the file's name): the Hecke algebra\nunder study is `H_3(R, q)`, i.e. the 3-strand case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.n_strands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.n_strands","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/spectral_sequence_h3_explicit.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Strand count of the Hecke algebra (manuscript: `H_3` ⇒ 3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.N","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/spectral_sequence_h3_explicit.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Neutron number `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.Z","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/spectral_sequence_h3_explicit.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Proton number `Z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/spectral_sequence_h3_explicit.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext","kind":"class","line":15,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/spectral_sequence_h3_explicit.lean#L15-L67","doc":"Abstract context for the `spectral_sequence_h3_explicit` claim —\nmanuscript-named typed fields below; sub-claims (i) the explicit\n`d_1`-differential, (ii) the explicit `d_2`-differential, and (iii) the\nconcretised page-identifications for `H_3(R, q)` are the three `Prop`\n**parameters**.\n\n**Parameterised 2026-09-13.**  The three sub-claims were `Prop`-valued\n*fields* with a `_holds` witness beside each — fields typed with the\n*universe* `Prop`, so the instance chose the proposition and\n`⟨True, trivial⟩` discharged all three.  Any\n`[SpectralSequenceH3ExplicitContext]`-conditional result was\nunconditional.  `QOU.ProofHygiene.SelfAssumingContexts` is the\nmachine-checked statement of why this shape is a defect *regardless of\nintent*: the carrier asserts nothing even as a conjecture, so it cannot\nserve as a conjectural witness either.\n\nAs parameters, the propositions are fixed by whoever writes the binder\nand appear in the type of every consumer, so a witness proves *that*\nproposition rather than one the instance picked.  The carrier stays\ninhabitable — it is a conjecture carrier and `Nonempty K ↔ C` is the\ncorrect semantics for one — but the vacuity is now visible in the type\ninstead of hidden in the instance.\n\n**No mathematical judgement is made here, deliberately.**  An earlier\nattempt encoded sub-claim (i) as `d₁ ∘ d₁ = 0`; that is true of *any*\ndifferential and is not the manuscript's claim, which is the explicit\n*formula*.  The same attempt encoded (iii) as page-stabilisation past\n`r = 3`, keying the index to `3` by association with `H_3` — which is\nthe Hecke **strand count**, not a spectral-sequence page index.  Both\nwere the author's call to make, not this file's; parameterising states\nthe shape without pre-empting either.  The conjectures are untouched\nand still open: no instance is supplied. ","signatureChunk":0}]}